test/check/error-pattern-uses.sumspec:9:15:
  |
9 | Page = Home | Editor (Doc * Mode)
  |               ^
warning: Page.Editor is never reached: neither __init nor any transition that can happen puts the app there

test/check/error-pattern-uses.sumspec:21:11:
   |
21 | __pattern Loop = App(Loop)
   |           ^
pattern Loop uses itself; a pattern may use another, but not in a cycle

test/check/error-pattern-uses.sumspec:25:6:
   |
25 | a :: W -> App(Link.Off)
   |      ^
pattern W takes 1 argument, but none is given

test/check/error-pattern-uses.sumspec:26:6:
   |
26 | b :: W(Mode.Viewing, Mode.Editing) -> App(Link.Off)
   |      ^
pattern W takes 1 argument, but 2 arguments are given

test/check/error-pattern-uses.sumspec:27:6:
   |
27 | c :: App(Link.Off, Link.On) -> App(Link.On)
   |      ^
a comma separates the arguments of a named pattern; join the arguments of a type with "*"

test/check/error-pattern-uses.sumspec:27:20:
   |
27 | c :: App(Link.Off, Link.On) -> App(Link.On)
   |                    ^
factor Link is written twice

test/check/error-pattern-uses.sumspec:28:6:
   |
28 | d :: W => Mode.Viewing -> Mode.Editing
   |      ^
W is a pattern, which goes where a pattern goes; a shared path is written with paths or a __path

test/check/error-pattern-uses.sumspec:29:6:
   |
29 | e :: Two => Link.Off -> Link.On
   |      ^
Two is a pattern, which goes where a pattern goes; a shared path is written with paths or a __path

test/check/error-pattern-uses.sumspec:30:6:
   |
30 | f :: Two.Home -> App(Link.On)
   |      ^
pattern Two is a whole pattern: nothing follows it after a dot

test/check/error-pattern-uses.sumspec:31:11:
   |
31 | g Id#n :: Picked(Item.Done) -> App(Link.On)
   |           ^
parameter i is the key of an element path, so its argument is one name (in pattern Picked, at 19:33)

test/check/error-pattern-uses.sumspec:32:6:
   |
32 | h :: Bad -> App(Link.On)
   |      ^
Of is not a variant of Link (in pattern Bad, at 20:26)

test/check/error-pattern-uses.sumspec:33:24:
   |
33 | k :: App(Page.Home) // Bad -> App(Link.On)
   |                        ^
Of is not a variant of Link (in pattern Bad, at 20:26)

test/check/error-pattern-uses.sumspec:34:6:
   |
34 | i :: Loop -> App(Link.On)
   |      ^
pattern Loop uses itself, so it can't be expanded

test/check/error-pattern-uses.sumspec:35:12:
   |
35 | j :: Page.{Editor | W(Mode.Viewing, Mode.Editing)} -> Page.Home
   |            ^
warning: j: this transition can never happen: its source needs Page.Editor, which is never reached

test/check/error-pattern-uses.sumspec:35:21:
   |
35 | j :: Page.{Editor | W(Mode.Viewing, Mode.Editing)} -> Page.Home
   |                     ^
a comma separates the arguments of a named pattern, not of a variant

